<article class="env-lemma" id="0FLW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FLW">Lemma <span data-tag="0FLW">50.3.1</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of affine schemes given by the ring map $R \to A$. Then $R\Gamma (X, \Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}) = \Omega ^\bullet _{A/R}$ in $D(R)$ and $H^ i_{dR}(X/S) = H^ i(\Omega ^\bullet _{A/R})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a> and Leray's acyclicity lemma (Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015E" data-tag="015E">13.16.7</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>